<description>
Move every small colored sprite into the enclosed holes of the large objects and erase the grey markers.

Input structure
- The background is the dominant color.
- Grey pixels are isolated marker noise.
- Some non-grey foreground components are large monochromatic objects with enclosed background holes.
- The remaining non-grey foreground components are source sprites outside those holes.

Rule
- Detect the enclosed background holes inside the large objects.
- Translate each source sprite without rotation or recoloring.
- Use every source sprite exactly once so the translated sprite masks exactly partition all hole cells.
- Clear the original source sprite cells and all grey marker pixels; preserve the large objects.

Key insight
- The destination is not chosen by color or position: the set of sprite shapes has a unique exact tiling of the enclosed holes.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "non-grey 4-connected source sprites s that are not holed objects",
  "dst": "enclosed background hole cells d inside large monochromatic objects",
  "match_cond": "translated s masks, with every s used once, partition all d cells exactly; multiple sprites may fill one connected hole",
  "transform": "clear original s locations and grey marker pixels; paint each d cell with the matched sprite color while preserving the holed objects"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
task_id: 184a9768
type: move_to_match

spec:
  grid: 20-25 rows x 20-26 cols, background BLACK
  containers:
    count: 1-2 monochromatic solid-rectangle objects with internal holes
    bbox: 6-16 rows x 8-13 cols; fills bbox completely (fill_ratio=1.0)
    holes_per_container: 2-4 disjoint 4-connected regions of background inside the container
    hole_shape: mostly rectangular; occasionally L/T-shaped (a union of 2 axis-aligned rectangles)
    hole_area: 1-18 per hole; wall thickness >= 1 between holes and to container edge
    container_colors: distinct from each other; may overlap with sprite colors
  sprites:
    count: 5-10 small rectangular (bbox-filling) monochromatic 4-connected components
    area: 1-18 per sprite; all sprites are axis-aligned rectangles
    colors: 3-5 distinct non-BLACK non-GREY colors; multiple sprites may share a color
    placement: scattered on background, outside containers, non-overlapping
  grey_markers:
    count: 6-11 isolated single-pixel GREY(5) cells scattered randomly on background
  tiling_constraint: total sprite area == total hole area; sprites tile all hole cells exactly once with unique solution
    (translated without rotation; multiple sprites may fill one hole)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size (20-25 x 20-26) and 1-2 container colors.
    2. For each container, choose bbox size and place on grid (non-overlapping, with margin).
    3. Design holes inside each container (2-4 per container, wall>=1 to edges and between holes).
       Holes are mostly rectangular; optionally one L-shaped hole (union of 2 rectangles).
    4. Partition each hole region into axis-aligned rectangles to define sprite shapes.
       Ensure the full tiling across ALL holes has a unique solution by construction
       (assign distinct shape-sets per hole so no cross-hole ambiguity arises).
    5. Assign 3-5 distinct non-BLACK non-GREY colors to sprites; allow color reuse.
    6. Build the output grid: containers with holes filled by colored sprites.
    7. Derive input: remove sprites from holes (restore background), scatter each sprite
